WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.220
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.689
That number is two one nine two David P..

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:09.080
More and more people asking about moving out
of the country.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.230
Take a listen to this.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.549
Hi, David.

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:17.260
So I've been so terrified of the possibility
of Trump getting another four years that I've

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:24.619
been thinking pretty seriously about how I
would try to the country lead the USA and

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:27.640
live in a different country if that were to
happen.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.540
Yeah, I just think I would be safer.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.970
So I'm wondering if you have any advice or
people who want to do that.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:43.789
Do you remember anything about your own immigration
from Argentina that bribe useful to somebody

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:47.420
who was thinking about immigrating away from
the United States?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.420
Well, yes.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.010
What I remember is that there is a reason
why most people don't do it.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:56.200
We he we you know, we've heard many times
before, if Bush gets reelected, I move to

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.200
Canada.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.200
If Obama gets reelected, I'm moving.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.550
I don't know where they would go.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:03.600
But in any case, most people don't do it because
it's insane.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.680
I mean, it's real.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.150
It's really a difficult thing.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:10.730
It's as someone who came to the United States
still young enough to quickly learn the language

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:11.730
and culture.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:16.320
It is a really big thing to abandon your home.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.630
And this is why, you know, we shouldn't take
lightly the fact that people are willing to

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.740
come to the United States, even illegally.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.210
Understand the cataclysmic change that this
represents from them.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.780
It is an an unimaginable change.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.720
And I would be lying if I said I'm thinking
of relocating permanently if Donald Trump

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:36.720
gets reelected.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.800
But the truth is that it is, and particularly
now with the mobile studio where I can basically

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.790
take have the exact same sound and video quality
no matter where I go.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.250
I am certainly thinking of if Trump gets reelected,
we'll be here covering the lame duck period.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.300
And of course, the the reelection the inauguration,
rather.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.410
But I am looking at spending some months doing
the show from somewhere else.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.420
And I understand that not everybody can do
that.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.420
Not everybody's jobs are mobile.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.300
Not everybody can afford it.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.840
But it is something I am looking at just to
get a break, just to get get get a break from

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.110
being in a place where constantly just idiocy
is happening.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.470
So I think that very few people are really
going to move out of the United States if

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:24.430
Trump is reelected, partially because it's
really cataclysmic change in one's life, partially

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.390
because it's really hard to do it.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.800
You can't just move to a lot of the places
that I think most Americans would look to

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.110
move to if they are trying to avoid Donald
Trump.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:41.280
But certainly I'd be lying if if if I said
it's not occurring to me to get a break from

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.890
the United States if Donald Trump does get
reelected.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.130
But we'll we're going to continue talking
about that.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:49.220
And I'm interested in hearing from the audience
about it.

